{% assign featured_products_collection = collections[section.settings.featured_collection] %}
{% assign collection_title = featured_products_collection.title %}
{% assign featured_products = featured_products_collection.products %}

{%- comment -%}
  bd 958r.3 — this line used to read:
      assign product_limit = section.settings.grid | times: section.settings.rows
  copied from sections/section-collection.liquid, but this section's schema defines neither
  `grid` nor `rows`, so product_limit evaluated to nil — AND the product loop below never
  applied it at all. The slider therefore rendered the WHOLE collection (Shopify caps
  collection.products at 50). Six of these sections on the homepage = 300 server-rendered
  product cards, ~8,680 element tags = 69% of the homepage DOM, which is the direct driver of
  the Style & Layout (1995ms) and Rendering (1255ms) main-thread buckets.
  Now driven by a real, editor-tunable setting and actually applied to the loop.

  MEASURED 2026-08-05 on the homepage, 50 -> 16 products per slider:
    HTML transfer      190.1KB -> 163.0KB per pageview  (-27KB)
    HTML uncompressed  2,244KB -> 1,386KB               (-859KB parse cost)
    DOM elements       11,877  -> 6,638                 (-44%)
    Desktop A/B (interleaved, n=8/arm): median score 61.0 -> 59.5, median LCP
    1.27s -> 1.60s, CLS 0.006 -> 0.011. All within run-to-run noise: NO
    demonstrated desktop performance gain. Desktop is bottlenecked on
    third-party JS (~9.75s main-thread across templates), not on DOM size.
  => DEFAULT IS 50, i.e. historical behaviour is preserved. Lower it per-section
     in the theme editor if you want the bandwidth/parse saving for low-end
     mobile; do NOT expect a PSI score change. Merchandising trade-off: fewer
     products browsable in the carousel.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign product_limit = section.settings.products_to_show | default: 50 -%}

{% if section.settings.is_custom_title_font %}
  {%- assign title_font = section.settings.custom_title_font -%}
{% else %}
  {%- assign title_font = section.settings.title_font.family -%}
{% endif %}

{% if section.settings.is_custom_product_title_font %}
  {%- assign product_title_font = section.settings.custom_product_title_font -%}
{% else %}
  {%- assign product_title_font = section.settings.product_title_font.family -%}
{% endif %}

{% if section.settings.is_custom_product_price_font %}
  {%- assign product_price_font = section.settings.custom_product_price_font -%}
{% else %}
  {%- assign product_price_font = section.settings.product_price_font.family -%}
{% endif %}

<div class="wrapper">
  <div class="data-section-id=" {{ section.id }} ">
    <div class="section-header text-center">
      {% comment %}<!-- replaced w/ dynamic 'block' <h2 class="h2--body rte section-header__title">New Arrivals</h2> -->{% endcomment %}
      <h2 class="h2--body rte section-header__title home__subtitle">{{ collection_title }}
      </h2>
      {% comment %}
        <div class="text-center"><a href="{{ featured_products_collection.url }}" class="collection-view-all">View All</a></div>
      {% endcomment %}
    </div>

    {%- if featured_products.size <= 6 -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Scope --productsCount to this section's id, NOT :root. Multiple
        instances of this section on the same page (e.g. Dyson landing
        with 3 featured-product blocks) all wrote to :root, so the LAST
        section's count overwrote the earlier ones — every grid then
        rendered as 1 column. Scoping to #shopify-section-{id} lets
        each section keep its own count.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <style>
        #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} {
          --productsCount: {{ featured_products.size }};
        }
      </style>
    <div class="collection-grid__box">
      {% for product in featured_products limit: product_limit %}
        <div class="collection-grid__item">
          {% render 'product-grid-item', product: product %}
        </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  {% else %}
    {% render 'collection-slider' products: featured_products, product_limit: product_limit %}
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if featured_products.size > 6 -%}
    <div class="btn-box text-center">
      <a href="{{ featured_products_collection.url }}" class="btn--outline uppercase">
        {{ 'collections.general.view_all' | t }}
      </a>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
</div></div>{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Collection Slider",
  "class": "collection-slider",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "title",
      "label": "Heading",
      "default": "Featured Collection Slider"
    }, {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "title_font_size",
      "min": 1,
      "max": 40,
      "step": 1,
      "label": "Title font size",
      "default": 28
    }, {
      "type": "collection",
      "id": "featured_collection",
      "label": "Select Collection"
    }, {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "products_to_show",
      "min": 4,
      "max": 50,
      "step": 2,
      "label": "Products to show",
      "info": "Products rendered into the HTML up front. Lower = smaller DOM/HTML. See the comment at the top of this file and bd 958r.3 for measured trade-offs.",
      "default": 50
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Collection Slider",
      "category": "Slider"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}